{"type":"delta","text":"Honest answer: I don't have specific data on your Commerce Cloud team's "}
{"type":"delta","text":"velocity, adoption milestones, sprint cadence, or rollout pattern in your "}
{"type":"delta","text":"connected enterprise layer. I can see some tenant context, but nothing that "}
{"type":"delta","text":"surfaces Commerce Cloud program metrics, team throughput, or adoption curves at "}
{"type":"delta","text":"that level of detail.\n"}
{"type":"delta","text":"What I'd want to know to give you a real answer: Is this in flight as a named "}
{"type":"delta","text":"program? If so, your program inventory and KPI dictionary should have phase, "}
{"type":"delta","text":"budget consumption, and current-vs-target metrics. If those aren't surfaced, "}
{"type":"delta","text":"that's actually a signal worth noting — programs without tracked KPIs tend to "}
{"type":"delta","text":"drift.\n"}
{"type":"delta","text":"If you can point me to what's actually in flight — timeline, sponsor, what "}
{"type":"delta","text":"\"adoption\" means in your context (GMV on platform, feature activation, merchant "}
{"type":"delta","text":"onboarding) — I can give you a sharper read on whether the pattern looks healthy "}
{"type":"delta","text":"or stalled relative to what I'd expect for a Commerce Cloud deployment at your "}
{"type":"delta","text":"scale.\n"}
{"type":"delta","text":"What's driving the question? That shapes whether you need a diagnostic on "}
{"type":"delta","text":"execution health or something else."}
{"type":"followups","followups":["Is Commerce Cloud tracked as a formal named program with a sponsor and documented KPIs, or is it currently running without that governance layer?","What does 'adoption' actually mean for your business — are we measuring GMV migration to the platform, merchant count activated, feature utilization rates, or something else entirely?","Do you have program metrics (timeline, budget burn, phase gates) surfaced somewhere that I should be looking at, or is that visibility gap itself part of what's concerning you?"]}
