iatives that failed, were paused indefinitely, or significantly underperformed in the last 5 years. Maintained as institutional memory. Source documents (post-mortems, status updates,...\n- change_failure_record.md: supports analytics but not real-time customer activation. 3. **Marketing's expected use never materialized.** The CMO's team continued to use Klaviyo's native segmentation rather than the data lake, because Klaviyo workflow integration was easier than data-lake-to-Klaviyo synchronization. 4. **Operating cost was higher than projected.** Snowflake and S3 costs ran $890K higher in year 1 than the business case projected, due to higher query volumes from...\n- it_leadership.json: id: person:apex:priya-iyer name: Priya Iyer title: VP, Digital & E-commerce Technology reports_to: person:apex:carlos-rivera tenure_in_role_years: 3 domains_owned: [\"e-commerce platform\",\"mobile app\",\"marketing technology\",\"site search\",\"personalization\"] team_size: 47 known_for: tightly aligned with the CMO; powerful internal voice on customer-facing investment","confidence":0.94},{"type":"WORLDVIEW","name":"Consulting displacement starts with the middle, not the top","id":"worldview:W5:008","detail":"","confidence":0.40486446},{"type":"WORLDVIEW","name":"AbarVa Positioning: The Evidence-Centric Operating System","id":"worldview:W4:016","detail":"","confidence":0.387185186},{"type":"WORLDVIEW","name":"Measure Realized Value, Not AI Activity","id":"worldview:W2:014","detail":"","confidence":0.386334211}]}
{"type":"delta","text":"The CMO's instinct is understandable but I'd revise the sequencing. \"Cheapest to "}
{"type":"delta","text":"activate\" and \"best first move\" aren't the same thing, and Einstein is a good "}
{"type":"delta","text":"example of why.\n"}
{"type":"delta","text":"The failure pattern I've seen repeatedly — and your own change record has a "}
{"type":"delta","text":"version of it with the CDP/data lake program — is that marketing-led activations "}
{"type":"delta","text":"stall because the data substrate underneath them isn't ready. Einstein "}
{"type":"delta","text":"Personalization and product recommendations are only as good as the behavioral "}
{"type":"delta","text":"signal and catalog data feeding them. If your item-location data is patchy or "}
{"type":"delta","text":"your Klaviyo integration isn't clean, you'll get mediocre output, Jennifer's "}
{"type":"delta","text":"team will revert to native segmentation (which is exactly what happened with the "}
{"type":"delta","text":"CDP), and Einstein becomes shelfware with the CIO blamed for it.\n"}
{"type":"delta","text":"The sequencing I'd defend: fix the data foundation first — even a 60-day sprint "}
{"type":"delta","text":"to validate what's actually flowing cleanly into Einstein's inputs — then "}
{"type":"delta","text":"activate. That's a small delay for a much higher success probability on the "}
{"type":"delta","text":"first visible win.\n"}
{"type":"delta","text":"The other thing worth naming: Priya Iyer owns the marketing tech stack and is "}
{"type":"delta","text":"tightly aligned with the CMO. If Priya is advocating for Einstein activation, "}
{"type":"delta","text":"that's political momentum worth using — but direct it toward a clean activation, "}
{"type":"delta","text":"not a fast one. Fast and visible is only valuable if it actually works.\n"}
{"type":"delta","text":"What's the current state of the behavioral data feeding Einstein? That's the "}
{"type":"delta","text":"pivot point."}
{"type":"followups","followups":["What does the current state of behavioral data feeding Einstein actually look like — is it the item-location data or the Klaviyo integration that's the known weak point, or is that unmapped?","If we do a 60-day data validation sprint first, how do we frame that to the CMO and Priya as a win rather than a delay — what's the internal narrative that keeps momentum?","What happens if we pilot Einstein on a single high-confidence segment or channel first while the data cleanup runs in parallel — does that satisfy the 'visible win' pressure without betting the whole program?"]}
{"type":"done"}

