{"type":"delta","text":"Before I shape the Move, I need to flag: I don't have your prior conversation "}
{"type":"delta","text":"turn in this session, so I don't have context on what my \"top recommendation\" "}
{"type":"delta","text":"was. I'll make a defensible call based on what's in your active program "}
{"type":"delta","text":"inventory and what I know about where Apex is right now. My top recommendation "}
{"type":"delta","text":"for Apex is the Contact Center AI program (apex-cc-ai-2026). It's in Phase 1, "}
{"type":"delta","text":"Jennifer Park is sponsoring it, David Okonjo is co-sponsoring. That dual CMO/COO "}
{"type":"delta","text":"ownership is actually good coalition structure for this type of bet. Here's the "}
{"type":"delta","text":"Move shape: SPONSOR STRUCTURE Primary: Jennifer Park (CMO) — owns the customer "}
{"type":"delta","text":"experience outcome. Co-sponsor: David Okonjo (COO) — owns the cost structure. "}
{"type":"delta","text":"Program lead: Priya Iyer already named. That's the right team, though Priya is "}
{"type":"delta","text":"also carrying CDP Activation, which is a bandwidth risk worth naming explicitly. "}
{"type":"delta","text":"SCOPE Phase 1 should target tier-1 contact deflection — password resets, order "}
{"type":"delta","text":"status, return initiation — not full conversational AI across all contact types. "}
{"type":"delta","text":"Constrained scope is what separates the programs that hit value in year one from "}
{"type":"delta","text":"the ones that get stuck in perpetual pilot. BUSINESS CASE Two levers: (1) cost — "}
{"type":"delta","text":"deflect 25-35% of tier-1 volume, translating to agent hour reduction or capacity "}
{"type":"delta","text":"redeployment; (2) CSAT — faster resolution on high-frequency low-complexity "}
{"type":"delta","text":"contacts. Don't build the case on both simultaneously. Pick cost as the primary "}
{"type":"delta","text":"metric with CSAT as the guard rail."}
